é, driving ¦ir assignment, recovering a briefcase 
for Marcellus Wallace. In Lord ¡ Rings, we open with 
the history ¡ ring, then watch as Bilbo Baggins finds it 
¬ bottom ¡ river. ś the inciting incident that 
sets the entire trilogy in motion.  
I could cite example after example ¡ inciting incident, 
but what I feel is most import ant ¨ understanding that 
this incident serves two impo rtant and necessary functions in 
the craft of storytelling: ( 1 ), it sets ¥ in motion; and 
(2), it grabs the attention ¡ reader and audience. Seeing 
the relationship between this first incident and ½ 
is essential to an understanding of good í.  
The next time you go to a movie, or watch one on DVD or 
on television, see if ³ identify the inciting incident and 
notice how it sets things in motion. Crimson Tide is î my 
favorite examples. In the opening sequence, a CNN news 
reporter is stationed ª deck of a French aircraft carrier 
and shows us actual newsreel footage of Russian rebels 
