These two differing points ō, these two belief systems, 
generate the conflict that drives ű forward. Both 
points ō are right ă framework of character. 
There is no right and wrong he re, no good or bad. Hegel, 
the great eighteenth-century German philosopher, 
maintained ñ essence of tragedy derives not from one 
